# movies-w6 -- W6-06-13: Movies & Credits > Play Movies is live when the
# player supplied movie files, and lists the campaign's movies that exist.
# The install's MOVIES0x.MIX are 4-byte stubs, so the run points the movie
# folder at the repo's test Bink (tests/data/movies/a01_f00e.bik, a copy of
# the decoder's bink_audio_rdft.bik fixture) unless RA2_MOVIE_DIR is already
# set by the player. Without any movie file the row stays greyed.
set movie_dir ../../tests/data/movies
set render_every 1
set on_quit continue
click button "Movies & Credits"
until 30 scene == "shell:Movies & Credits"
click button "Play Movies"
until 30 scene == movies                                 @W6-06-13
require scene == movies
assert movie_count >= 1                                  @W6-06-13
shot movies
click movie0
until 120 scene == movies                                @W6-06-13
click back
until 30 scene == "shell:Movies & Credits"               @W6-06-13
end
